---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';

const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/obzly/obzly';
---

<Marketing
	title="Disclaimer · Obzly"
	description="Obzly is free, open-source software provided as is, without warranty. What that means for you, your data and the third-party names on this site."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Disclaimer</div>
			<h1>Disclaimer</h1>
			<p class="checked">Last updated 6 November 2026</p>
		</div>

		<div class="legal">
			<div class="pick us legal-summary">
				<h2>In short</h2>
				<p>
					Obzly is free, open-source software provided <b>as is</b>. You run it at your own risk, and nobody who works
					on it is liable for any loss that comes from using it. The <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache License 2.0</a> is what legally applies; this page explains it
					in plain words and doesn't change it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2 id="no-warranty">No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				Obzly comes with no promise of any kind. Nobody guarantees that it works, that it suits your purpose, that it's
				secure, free of errors or always available, or that it won't lose or damage data. Deciding whether it's right for
				you, and how you use it, is your responsibility. Section 7 of the licence says:
			</p>
			<blockquote>
				<p>
					7. Disclaimer of Warranty. Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, Licensor provides the Work
					(and each Contributor provides its Contributions) on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY
					KIND, either express or implied, including, without limitation, any warranties or conditions of TITLE,
					NON-INFRINGEMENT, MERCHANTABILITY, or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. You are solely responsible for
					determining the appropriateness of using or redistributing the Work and assume any risks associated with Your
					exercise of permissions under this License.
				</p>
			</blockquote>

			<h2 id="no-liability">No liability for losses</h2>
			<p>
				The Obzly contributors aren't liable for any damage or loss from using Obzly, or from being unable to use it.
				That includes lost or corrupted data, lost revenue or profit, downtime, missed or late alerts, and the cost of
				recovering, even if someone was told it could happen. Section 8 of the licence says:
			</p>
			<blockquote>
				<p>
					8. Limitation of Liability. In no event and under no legal theory, whether in tort (including negligence),
					contract, or otherwise, unless required by applicable law (such as deliberate and grossly negligent acts) or
					agreed to in writing, shall any Contributor be liable to You for damages, including any direct, indirect,
					special, incidental, or consequential damages of any character arising as a result of this License or out of
					the use or inability to use the Work (including but not limited to damages for loss of goodwill, work stoppage,
					computer failure or malfunction, or any and all other commercial damages or losses), even if such Contributor
					has been advised of the possibility of such damages.
				</p>
			</blockquote>

			<h2 id="your-data">Your data and operations</h2>
			<p>Obzly runs on infrastructure you choose and control, so running it well is up to you:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<b>Backups.</b> Back up Postgres and your object storage, and test restoring them. See <a href="/docs/operations/backup-restore/">Backup and restore</a> and <a href="/docs/operations/disaster-recovery/">Disaster recovery</a>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Deletion is permanent.</b> Retention, quota and delete settings remove data for good. Check them before you
					change them.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Security.</b> Keep Obzly and what it runs on patched and locked down. See <a href="/docs/operations/upgrade/">Upgrade</a> and the <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/SECURITY.md#hardening-notes-for-operators`}>hardening notes</a>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Capacity.</b> Size it for your load and watch it. See <a href="/docs/getting-started/requirements/">System requirements</a>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Upgrades.</b> Read the release notes and try an upgrade outside production first.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Personal data.</b> Logs, traces and metrics can contain personal or sensitive data. Meeting privacy, data
					protection and retention laws for what you collect is your responsibility.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Alerts aren't a guarantee.</b> Alerts, synthetic monitors and dashboards can be late, wrong or not delivered.
					Don't make them the only safeguard for anything where a missed alert could cause harm.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="third-parties">Third-party names and links</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Grafana, Loki, Mimir, Tempo, Elastic, OpenObserve, SigNoz, Datadog, Splunk, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry,
					Kubernetes, AWS, Azure and other product and company names on this site are trademarks of their owners. They're
					used only to describe compatibility and comparisons.
				</li>
				<li>Obzly isn't affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by any of them.</li>
				<li>
					The <a href="/compare/">comparison pages</a> describe each vendor from its own public docs and pricing on the
					date shown. Products change, so check the vendor's current pages before you decide.
				</li>
				<li>
					Links to other sites are for convenience. Obzly doesn't control or endorse their content.
				</li>
				<li>
					On <a href="/donate/">Support Obzly</a>, you choose and give to a charity directly. Obzly doesn't recommend,
					vet or receive money for any charity or NGO.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="support">Support</h2>
			<p>
				Help in GitHub <a href={`${GITHUB}/issues`}>Issues</a> and <a href={`${GITHUB}/discussions`}>Discussions</a> is
				given on a best-effort basis by the community and maintainers. There's no service-level agreement, and no
				obligation to answer, fix or ship anything.
			</p>

			<p class="fine" style="padding-bottom:64px">
				This page is a plain-language summary for convenience, not legal advice. If it differs from the Apache License
				2.0, the licence applies. Questions? Ask in <a href="/community/">the community</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Marketing>
